{"wrong":"very agree","fix":"strongly agree","why":"very不能直接修饰动词"}
{"wrong":"this restaurant food","fix":"this restaurant's food","why":"餐厅与食物之间需用所有格"}
{"wrong":"so good than","fix":"as good as","why":"同级比较用not as...as"}

{"wrong":"very agree","fix":"totally agree","why":"agree不能用very修饰"}
{"wrong":"this restaurant food","fix":"this restaurant's food","why":"表示餐厅的食物需用所有格"}
{"wrong":"not so good than","fix":"not as good as","why":"否定的同级比较用not as...as"}

{"wrong":"There was a lot of people","fix":"There were a lot of people","why":"people是复数，谓语应使用were"}
{"wrong":"everyone become","fix":"everyone became","why":"叙述过去的事情，动词应使用过去式"}
{"wrong":"a really fun experience","fix":"a really fun experience","why":"“a fun experience”中冠词位置不当"}
